claims.statement_original:
Consider the over-parameterized scalar-on-tensor regression under Gaussian ensemble design. Denote $df=\sum_{i=1}^d(p_i-r_i)r_i+\prod_{i=1}^d r_i$ and suppose $n\ge c(d)\left(\frac{\|\mathcal X^*\|_{\mathrm F}^2+\sigma^2}{\lambda^2}\left((\prod_{i=1}^d p_i)^{1/2}+df\right)\right)$ for some constant $c(d)$. Then with probability at least $1-\underline p^{-C}$ for some $C>0$,

• $\mathcal X^0$ returned from Algorithm 2 satisfies the initialization conditions in Theorems 1 and 2;

• consider RGD and RGN initialized with $\mathcal X^0$, then as long as $t_{\max}\ge\log\left(\frac{\lambda\sqrt{n/df}}{c_1(d)\sigma}\right)\vee0$ for RGD or $t_{\max}\ge\log\log\left(\frac{\lambda\sqrt{n/df}}{c_2(d)\sigma}\right)\vee0$ for RGN, we have the output of RGD or RGN satisfies $\|\mathcal X^{t_{\max}}-\mathcal X^*\|_{\mathrm F}\le c_3(d)\sigma\sqrt{df/n}$.

Consider the rank-1 tensor-on-tensor regression under Gaussian ensemble design (13). Denote $df=\sum_{i=1}^{d+m}p_i$ and suppose $\lambda>C'\sigma$ for some $C'>0$. If $n\ge c(d,m)\left(\frac{\lambda^2+\sigma^2}{\lambda^2}\left((\prod_{i=1}^d p_i)^{1/2}+\overline p\right)+\frac{\sigma^4}{\lambda^4}\left(\prod_{i=d+1}^{d+m}p_i+\overline p\right)\right)$ for some constant $c(d,m)$ depending on $d$ and $m$ only, where $\overline p=\max_{k=1,\ldots,d+m}p_i$. Then with probability at least $1-\underline p^{-C}$ for some $C>0$,

• $\mathcal X^0$ returned from Algorithm 4 satisfies the initialization conditions in Theorems 1 and 2;

• Considering RGD and RGN initialized with $\mathcal X^0$, as long as $t_{\max}\ge\log\left(\frac{\lambda\sqrt{n/df}}{c_1(d,m)\sigma}\right)\vee0$ for RGD or $t_{\max}\ge\log\log\left(\frac{\lambda\sqrt{n/df}}{c_2(d,m)\sigma}\right)\vee0$ for RGN, we have the output of RGD or RGN satisfies $\|\mathcal X^{t_{\max}}-\mathcal X^*\|_{\mathrm F}\le c_3(d,m)\sigma\sqrt{df/n}$.
